{{Term/Store|Naydra's Scale|Naydra's Scales|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Naydra's Scale}}<br/>This precious scale fell from the blue spirit Naydra. It contains a bitter cold within. You can use it in cooking, but just eating it seems like a waste.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Naydra's Scale}}<br/>This precious scale contains supercooled air inside. Attach it to a weapon to greatly increase its attack power. It can be cooked, but just eating it seems like a waste.|Inventory|TotK}}</ref>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Naydra's Scales can be collected from the [[Dragon]] [[Naydra]], who rests atop [[Mount Lanayru]]. After defeating [[Malice Naydra]] and freeing the Dragon, [[Link]] will be able to strike her anywhere on her body and retrieve a Scale. The first time that Link strikes Naydra, she will yield a Scale regardless of where she was struck. To subsequently obtain a Scale from Naydra, Link must strike the main portion of her body. A Scale can also be found in a [[Treasure Chest]] beneath a stone slab above the northern entrance to the [[Library]] at [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]].

Link must place a Scale inside the [[Spring of Wisdom]] to complete the [[Shrine Quest]] "[[The Spring of Wisdom]]". Doing so will yield the way to [[Jitan Sa'mi Shrine]].

[[Cooking]] with Naydra's Scales will add 90 seconds to the [[Meal]]'s [[Added Effect]] and guarantee a critical dish. They can also be used at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] to make [[Light Blue Dye]].

Naydra's Scales are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Naydra's Scale}}

